From f056a12bb2cd57ce5b3ae7648ba1e8d8c477e534 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lateautumn233 <lateautumn233@foxmail.com>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 00:16:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] virtio-gpu: Add Gunyah Resource Manager support for
 memparcel handling

This patch series introduces support for the Gunyah Resource Manager (RM) in the virtio-gpu driver, enabling the guest to accept memparcels shared by the host. Key changes include:

- Addition of `gunyah_handle` and `gunyah_accepted` fields in `virtio_gpu_object_vram` to manage memparcel acceptance.
- Implementation of `gunyah_guest_mem_accept` and `gunyah_guest_mem_release` functions to handle memparcel acceptance and release.
- Modifications to the blob creation and mapping functions to integrate Gunyah RM interactions, including error handling and logging for debugging.
- New Kconfig options to enable Gunyah RM probing and guest-side memparcel acceptance.
- Introduction of `gh_probe.c` and `gunyah_guest.c` files to manage Gunyah RM communication and operations.

These changes enhance the virtio-gpu driver's capability to work in environments utilizing the Gunyah hypervisor, improving resource management and guest performance.
